IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Defence Force Retirement and Death Benefits (Pension Increases) Act 1976
-- (Cth). Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01465.txt (compilation No.
-- 1, 10 December 2015). Part II is deemed to have commenced on 1 July 1973,
-- Part III on 1 July 1975. Seat: the pensioner, widow or child.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Scheme` IS ONE OF
    -- Part II, ss 6-7
    `a DFRB pension`
    -- ss 6(1), 7(1): excluded
    `a DFRB pension for an eligible child`
    -- Part III, ss 19-21
    `a DFRDB pension benefit`

-- Part II: the increase for 1973-74 (s 6), or a prescribed year (s 7).
DECLARE `Increase year` IS ONE OF
    `1973-74`
    `1974-75`
    `1975-76`

-- ss 10, 11, 21: whether the increase is scaled by months, and from when.
DECLARE `Period kind` IS ONE OF
    `not scaled`
    `counted from the day after the retirement or death`
    `counted from the day the pension became payable`

DECLARE `Pension 1976` HAS
    `scheme`                                            IS A `Scheme`
    `increase year`                                     IS A `Increase year`
    -- ss 6(3), 7(3), 18(2): A and B (CPI), C and D (average weekly earnings)
    `A`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `B`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `C`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `D`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    -- ss 6(2), 7(2): the non-contributory portion (s 8); s 20(2), 21(4): the
    -- annual pension benefit (for a child, the additional pension)
    `the amount the percentage applies to`              IS A NUMBER
    `period kind`                                       IS A `Period kind`
    `the retirement, death or first payment was on`     IS A DATE
    -- ss 10(3), 11(3), 21(1)
    `it became payable on`                              IS A DATE

§ `Rules`

-- ss 5(4), 18(4): a fraction of a tenth of 1% under one-half is disregarded,
-- otherwise treated as a tenth.
@ref ss 5(4), 18(4)
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded to a tenth` x MEANS FLOOR (x TIMES 10 PLUS 1/2) DIVIDED BY 10

-- ss 6(3), 7(3): the lower of 1.4 times the CPI rise and the earnings rise,
-- each as a percentage. s 18(2): Part III uses the CPI rise alone.
@ref ss 6(3), 7(3), 18(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1976`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prescribed percentage for` p MEANS
    IF p's `scheme` EQUALS `a DFRDB pension benefit`
    THEN `rounded to a tenth` cpi
    ELSE `rounded to a tenth` (IF 14/10 TIMES cpi AT MOST awe THEN 14/10 TIMES cpi ELSE awe)
    WHERE
        cpi MEANS (p's `A` MINUS p's `B`) TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY p's `B`
        awe MEANS (p's `C` MINUS p's `D`) TIMES 100 DIVIDED BY p's `D`

-- ss 6(1), 7(1): both indices rose; s 19: the CPI rose.
@ref ss 6(1), 7(1), 19
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1976`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the indices rose` p IF
        p's `A` GREATER THAN p's `B`
    AND (p's `scheme` EQUALS `a DFRDB pension benefit` OR p's `C` GREATER THAN p's `D`)

-- The 30 June that ends the counted period: 1973 for s 10, 1974 for s 11 in
-- 1974-75, 1975 for s 11 in 1975-76 and for s 21.
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1976`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day after the period ends for` p MEANS
    IF p's `scheme` EQUALS `a DFRDB pension benefit`
    THEN Date 1 7 1975
    ELSE CONSIDER p's `increase year`
         WHEN `1973-74` THEN Date 1 7 1973
         WHEN `1974-75` THEN Date 1 7 1974
         WHEN `1975-76` THEN Date 1 7 1975

-- ss 10(2), 11(2), 21(3): over 21 months for s 10, 12 otherwise.
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1976`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the divisor for` p MEANS
    IF p's `scheme` EQUALS `a DFRB pension` AND p's `increase year` EQUALS `1973-74` THEN 21 ELSE 12

GIVEN s IS A DATE, e IS A DATE, k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`whole months from` s `to` e `counted` k MEANS
    IF `add months` s (k PLUS 1) AT MOST e
    THEN `whole months from` s `to` e `counted` (k PLUS 1)
    ELSE k

-- ss 10(2), (4)-(5), 11(2), (4)-(5), 21(3), (5)-(6): whole months, a part
-- month of at least half its days counting as one, and at least 1.
@ref ss 10(4)-(5), 11(4)-(5), 21(5)-(6)
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1976`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months for` p MEANS
    IF counted LESS THAN 1 THEN 1 ELSE counted
    WHERE
        e MEANS `the day after the period ends for` p
        start MEANS
            IF p's `period kind` EQUALS `counted from the day after the retirement or death`
            THEN p's `the retirement, death or first payment was on` PLUS 1
            ELSE p's `the retirement, death or first payment was on`
        m MEANS `whole months from` start `to` e `counted` 0
        partStart MEANS `add months` start m
        partDays MEANS Day e MINUS Day partStart
        monthDays MEANS Day (`add months` start (m PLUS 1)) MINUS Day partStart
        counted MEANS IF partDays TIMES 2 AT LEAST monthDays AND partDays GREATER THAN 0 THEN m PLUS 1 ELSE m

-- ss 10(3), 11(3): no increase for an s 82ZB pension (counted from the day it
-- became payable) that became payable after 15 June before the period ends;
-- s 21(1): for any scaled Part III benefit (changed after the independent
-- pass).
@ref ss 10(3), 11(3), 21(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1976`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it came too late` p IF
        (   p's `period kind` EQUALS `counted from the day the pension became payable`
         OR (    p's `scheme` EQUALS `a DFRDB pension benefit`
             AND NOT (p's `period kind` EQUALS `not scaled`)))
    AND p's `it became payable on` GREATER THAN (`the day after the period ends for` p MINUS 16)

@ref ss 6-11, 18-21
@export default The increase in my annual pension under the Defence Force Retirement and Death Benefits (Pension Increases) Act 1976 (Cth): for a DFRB pension (Part II), in 1973-74 (s 6) and each of 1974-75 and 1975-76 (s 7), if both the CPI and average weekly earnings rose, the lower of 1.4 times the CPI rise and the earnings rise, rounded to a tenth of 1%, applied to the non-contributory portion of the pension (s 8), scaled by months for a pension that began recently (ss 10, 11: over 21 months to 30 June 1973, or 12); for a DFRDB pension benefit (Part III), the CPI rise from March 1974 to March 1975 applied to the annual benefit, scaled by months for a retirement or death from 1 July 1974 (ss 19-21). Nil for a DFRB child's pension, or a pension that became payable after 15 June of the year. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Pension 1976`  @desc The scheme and year, the index numbers, the amount, and any recent start
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my 1976 Act increase for` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's `scheme` EQUALS `a DFRB pension for an eligible child` THEN 0
        IF NOT (`the indices rose` p) THEN 0
        IF `it came too late` p THEN 0
        IF p's `period kind` EQUALS `not scaled` THEN full
        OTHERWISE full TIMES `the months for` p DIVIDED BY `the divisor for` p
    WHERE
        full MEANS `the prescribed percentage for` p DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES p's `the amount the percentage applies to`
